      "role": "user",
      "content": "Look, I'm not asking for a miracle, I'm just trying to survive this quarter. If I go to the board and tell them we need to push the Q3 launch back another two months just to build a \"robust\" middleware layer, I'm going to get fired and this whole project might get scrapped entirely.\n\nIf I tell them that we've assessed the technical risks and we have a plan to manage the data integrity via a lightweight adapter for the initial rollout, would that be a fair assessment of the situation? Can we honestly say the integration is viable for the launch phase if we commit to fixing the technical debt immediately after? I need to know if I can confidently greenlight this to the stakeholders.",
